WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Donald Trump has tweeted
negatively about you,

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.570 line:92%
but you're in excellent company.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.874
But one of the things was he -
you predicted on election nigh

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
a recession, which has not
come to pass.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is what he keeps
hammering home.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I retracted that
three days later.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Three days later.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Three days after the election
saying, "Okay, I did

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you're not supposed to do
which was I let --

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.354 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Motivated reasoning."

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.624
I said, "A terrible thing ha
just happened," which did,

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I let myself indulge mysel
by saying,

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.864
"It's going to lead to immediate
bad results on all fronts.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then three days later, I said,
"You know, actually Trump

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
is probably going to increas
the budget deficit

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:36.936 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and the budget deficit

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
is probably gonna give
the economy a bit of a jolt.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So it's actually --

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.542
We're not gonna have a recession
right away

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:46.713
and Trump might actually preside
over somewhat faster growth.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.715 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So, yeah, I had a bad --

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
I much regret
that election-night statement,

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know, I admitted
I was wrong

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.688 line:92%
and tried to learn from it

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.125
-I think when the Presiden
is wrong, he admits it, too.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's what
you guys have in common.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah, right.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.198
-We always say that's what Trump
and Krugman have in common

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.399 line:92%
They own up to their mistakes.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fix that comment
with a Sharpie.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.238 line:92%
-Hey, I want to talk about this.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously tonight
is the Iowa caucuses.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.845
There's a lot of writing about
how, you know, the Democrats

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:22.449
are putting everything at risk
with very progressive ideas.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yet you point out

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
that progressive ideas
are actually very popular.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will you explain
what the idea is?

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.023 size:84% position:42%
It's very popular with
the majority of people.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:30.723 line:92%
-Yeah. For the most part,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.626
if you ask people, "Should taxes
on the rich go up?"

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.594 line:92%
Overwhelming support for that.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.198
If you ask people, "Should the
government spend more or les

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:40.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Social Security
and Medicare?"

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
Overwhelming majority say,
"Spend more."

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
The public is actually kind of
left of center.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:49.409
I have to admit, it makes me
a little bit nervous that --

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, one of the things in
"Arguing With Zombies,"

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:56.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the book, I talk
about the Republican habit

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
of portraying anything that yo
try to do

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.120 line:92%
to make life a little bit better

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
as saying, "Oh,
that's socialism,"

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.923 size:75% position:38% line:92%
which is ridiculous.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.193
I'm a little bit nervous about
the idea of having somebody say,

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:07.894 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Yeah, it is socialism.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a socialist,"
when he actually isn't.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bernie Sanders is a social
Democrat, he's left of center,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's a little bit further left
of center

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
than others in the party,
but I --

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.607 line:92%
It may be brilliant to just play

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
right into the Republican
framing of it,

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it might also
be a problem.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it will be interestin
to see.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.314 line:92%
It's a delight to have you

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
Thank you.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.017 line:92%
-That's Paul Krugman, everybody.

